application responsiveness is required  for a good user experience  no matter how nice your ui looks if the  application is slow users are going to  be frustrated many times database  performance is the cause of application  slowdowns slow database queries result  in slow application requests  cloud spanner recently launched query  insights to assist users in diagnosing  performance issues with their queries  let me show you how easy it is to use  query insights to help diagnose query  performance issues in spanner  [Music]  imagine that you get an alert in the  middle of the night your database is  using too much cpu  now you need to find out why  if you've worked with databases long you  know how much of a pain it can be to  pinpoint the root cause of database  slowdowns  but if you start your performance  investigation looking for problematic  queries you're going to be faster  resolving the issue  this is why we've developed query  insights  query insights is a set of pre-built  dashboards which makes it very easy to  visualize spikes in query performance  so developers and dbas alike can easily  drill down to the problematic query or  queries  as a spanner user let's say you get that  alert about high cpu  the alert will link you to the  monitoring chart and sure enough your  spanner instance is using an unusually  high amount of cpu  this confirms that there could be  inefficient queries running during that  time window  now you click into query insights  here you find both the cpu usage and the  top queries consuming that cpu in that  time window  the top queries help you identify the  problematic query or queries  there's some other information about the  queries as well  for example how many times that query  shape was executed  maybe a single slow query caused that  spike in cpu or maybe hundreds of  executions of a faster query caused it  either way now you can drill down and  point to exactly which query or queries  could be causing the issue  then you can click into the queries and  analyze them to find out more  information such as how many rows were  scanned versus returned or the latency  of requests  in my case i found an expensive query  that gets a random set of 100 rows from  the players table  i can now refactor how this is handled  to improve the performance of these  requests  now whether you found a slow query that  needs to be rewritten  or faster queries that might need to be  cached so you don't make the requests as  often query insights helped you get to  this point quickly  making sure your database is performing  well is critical to the success of your  application  cloud spanner query insights was  developed to help you find a poorly  performing queries quickly  and the best part is you don't need to  do anything to start using query  insights it's enabled by default  it is worth noting that only queries and  dml are supported by query insights  this means that requests made using  spanner mutations are not available  if you are using queries in dml for your  application workload on cloud spanner go  ahead  check out query insights to find out  which queries might be slowing down your  database  [Music]
 

